# core-vendor.manifest — the pin. Names ONE commit of
# agenticapps-eu/agenticapps-workflow-core and a sha256 per file. Machine-read
# by bin/resolve-core-artifact.sh, by bin/materialise-core-artifacts.sh, by
# install.sh, and by migrations/run-tests.sh. Do NOT hand-edit a sha: re-pin by
# recomputing every entry at the new commit.
#
# core_commit is a COMMIT, not a branch. A core checkout is a live workspace and
# may sit mid-change on a feature branch, and origin/main can advance BETWEEN
# two commands. Resolve it ONCE and take every file from that one revision — a
# per-file rev-parse is how, in a sibling host, the gate and its harness once
# ended up from different commits.
#
# ONE commit covers EVERY file listed, and every file this repo takes from core
# is listed. Consistency among the entries present is not sufficient: a manifest
# naming three of five files is internally consistent while recording nothing
# about the two it omits.
#
# Advancing core_commit therefore means RE-VERIFYING the files already listed at
# the new revision, not just appending the new ones.
#
# ── what this host does NOT take from core ───────────────────────────────────
#
# Five files, not seven. claude-workflow pins two more; this host takes neither,
# and pinning a file it does not use would be provenance for nothing:
#
#   run-plan-review.sh      — absent from this repo. This host's §18 review
#     PRODUCER is a skill, skills/opencode-openspec-change-review, which drives
#     bin/reviewer-cli.sh itself. There is no producer script to publish.
#
#   install-shared-artifact.sh — install.sh carries its own arbitration instead,
#     in the marker-delimited `gate-version-arbitration` and
#     `reviewer-cli-version-arbitration` regions that the test suite sources by
#     name. Adopting core's installer is a separate change with its own tests;
#     it is NOT a thing this repo silently takes from core today.
#
# ── two categories, deliberately different (ADR-0047, ported from claude) ────
#
# RESOLVED — install.sh publishes these into the shared ~/.agenticapps/bin/.
#   They are NOT committed here any more. Vendoring them is what this change
#   removed: the runtime never read the committed copies — every consumer
#   prefers ~/.agenticapps/bin — so they existed only to feed the installer, and
#   they drifted. On 2026-07-31 this repo still carried gate 1.3.1 against
#   core's 2.0.0 and wrapper 1.1.0 against 1.2.0, having missed the release in
#   which reviews became advisory.
#
#   They still land at bin/, but as a gitignored CACHE regenerated by
#   bin/materialise-core-artifacts.sh — see that script for why the path had to
#   stay. A cached byte cannot drift: a wrong one fails the resolver's sha256
#   check and nothing lands.
#
# VENDORED — committed on disk, each for a reason it cannot be resolved:
#   resolve-core-artifact.sh is the bootstrap and cannot resolve itself; the two
#   conformance harnesses are executed from the repo by CI. Pinned anyway, so
#   the manifest's claim to list EVERY file taken from core is true rather than
#   convenient.
#
# ── the pin ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ef030d0 is core's main at the merge of core PR #49. It carries gate 2.0.0 and
# wrapper 1.2.0, plus core spec 1.4.0 / §20: a conformance harness that scored
# nothing is no longer green. A named target that is absent, empty or unreadable
# is now reported as `UNSCOREABLE <label> — <reason>` and fails, instead of
# printing `SKIP (not found)` / `TOTAL: 0 passed, 0 failed` and exiting 0.
#
# §20 matters to THIS host more than to the others, because this host is the one
# that sweeps the family. `tools/change-gate-conformance.sh --family` scores
# every sibling's bin/openspec-change-gate.sh. Once claude-workflow stopped
# vendoring one, the old harness filtered the missing path away and reported
# success over one fewer host — quietly narrower, not visibly broken. The §20
# harness declares `COVERAGE: scored N of M` and names what it skipped, so a
# pin-and-resolve host reads as *resolvable from pin, not attempted* rather than
# as nothing at all.
#
# This is the first pin this repo has ever had, so there are no prior entries to
# re-verify against. All five sha256s below were computed from ef030d0 directly
# (`git show ef030d0:<core-path> | shasum -a 256`), and the three files kept on
# disk were replaced with exactly those bytes.
core_repo=agenticapps-eu/agenticapps-workflow-core
core_commit=ef030d0430e6c0df6dc13ab567baab3f9e006dbe

# RESOLVED at install time — cached at bin/, gitignored, never committed.
file=bin/openspec-change-gate.sh sha256=4ad996cb7f95ebc45c35177eaad70781c23f166fb14283dc693a8ecc31476780
file=bin/reviewer-cli.sh sha256=9a26ebcda9f8c7e3839778337c1b56a4a421610735c08b8b5de1bb528397b11a

# VENDORED on disk — pinned so the copies are checkable against a fixed commit.
file=bin/resolve-core-artifact.sh sha256=1274598c07c0853b91c08d9b27da85d46cc754eff57b9c456cb79f293caf11ac
file=tools/change-gate-conformance.sh sha256=9ddfd5d641464920a4240c656384db722b3b7738768b09cc2a0beb2a2c3aeb21
file=tools/reviewer-cli-conformance.sh sha256=f5161c8b7025e889eec0c78c3b0d6091d51e630ee2b5585d6e7c721089855011
